@style(IDocDemo)
@title(Science: chemistry, medical imaging, physics and proofs)

Every block on this page is live in the preview. Each feature gets one line and one working example; the block is also what prints in the PDF.

@section(Chemistry: molecules and balanced equations)

Draw a molecule from its SMILES string, or balance a chemical equation to the smallest whole-number coefficients.

@chem
CCO
C3H8 + O2 -> CO2 + H2O
@end

@b{Molecules.} A line in SMILES notation is drawn as a 2-D skeletal structure with its formula underneath.

@chem
CC(=O)O
@end

@b{Equations.} A line with -> (or =) and + is an equation, balanced for you.

@chem
Fe + O2 -> Fe2O3
@end

@b{A caption.} A name: line becomes the caption.

@chem
name: Ethanol
CCO
@end

@b{A graded exercise.} expect= is the balanced equation the student must reach.

Balance the combustion of hydrogen.
@chem(id=h2o, expect="2H2 + O2 -> 2H2O")
H2 + O2 -> H2O
@end

@b{Graded.} With expect= the balanced result of the student's equation is compared with the key, and a correctly balanced equation earns the mark however it is spaced.

@section(Medical images: CT, MRI and DICOM)

View, measure and grade CT, MRI and other DICOM studies in the document, de-identified in your browser before anything is kept.

@dicom(src=phantom)
layout 1x2
series 2 window=lung slice=31
series 2 window=soft slice=31
@end

@b{The view, one line each.} layout, series with window= and slice=, point, length and roi lines; every click in the card writes a line.

@dicom(src=phantom)
series 2 window=soft slice=31
point 58,78 label=lesion
@end

@b{Your own study.} Drop a DICOM folder or CD onto the card: it is de-identified to DICOM PS3.15 Annex E and saved as a .bvol block, which src= then names.

@dicom(src=phantom)
@end

@b{3-D and presets.} A pane takes plane=3d with yaw=, pitch= and cut=; a preset line (bone, soft, lung, vessels, skin, mr) sets the transfer function.

@dicom(src=phantom)
preset bone
@end

@b{A graded question.} id=, pts=, expect= in millimetres: hotspot(lesion)=solution ±8mm, length(L1)=42±2mm, roi(liver)~solution dice>=0.85; the key is the @@solution section.

@dicom(src=phantom, id=q3, pts=10, expect="hotspot(lesion)=solution ±8mm")
series 2 window=lung slice=31
@solution
series 2 slice 31 point 58,78 label=lesion
@end

@b{Graded.} The server marks the student's view lines in millimetres against the @@solution key: a point within its distance, a length within its tolerance, an outline by its overlap (Dice).

@section(Physics simulations with sliders)

An animated physics system (pendulum, projectile, spring, orbit or double pendulum) with live sliders for its settings and a readout of energy and period.

@sim
system: pendulum
length: 1.2
gravity: 9.81
angle: 35
@end

@b{Choose the system.} system: pendulum, projectile, spring, orbit or double-pendulum.

@sim
system: projectile
speed: 20
angle: 45
@end

@b{Starting values.} Each line name: value sets one setting.

@sim
system: spring
mass: 1
k: 20
x0: 0.5
@end

@b{Hand in the settings.} pts= makes it work to hand in: the student hands in the settings they reached and a teacher marks them.

Set the pendulum to a 2 s period.
@sim(id=period2, pts=2)
system: pendulum
@end

@b{Graded.} Not marked automatically.

@section(Proofs students write, checked by the kernel)

Students write a proof one step per line, each step with its reason, and IDoc's own proof kernel checks every step as they type and again for the mark.

@lab(prove, id=p1, pts=6, goal="(a+b)^2 = a^2 + 2ab + b^2")
@solution
(a+b)^2 = (a+b)(a+b) by ring
        = a^2 + 2ab + b^2 by ring
@end

@b{Steps and reasons.} Each line is a = b (or <=, <, >=) with by and a reason: ring (algebra), sum (the definition of a sum), IH (the induction hypothesis).

@lab(prove, id=p0, goal="2(a+b) = 2a + 2b")
@end

@b{Induction.} induction n then a step: chain proves a statement for every n; a base case the kernel can compute may be left out.

@lab(prove, id=p2, pts=8, partial, goal="2 sum_{i=0}^{n} i = n(n+1)")
@solution
induction n
step: 2 sum_{i=0}^{n+1} i = 2 (sum_{i=0}^{n} i + (n+1)) by sum
  = 2 sum_{i=0}^{n} i + 2(n+1) by ring
  = n(n+1) + 2(n+1) by IH
  = (n+1)(n+2) by ring
@end

@b{Boolean algebra.} bool: each step names the one law it uses (absorption, De Morgan, distributive, consensus, ...), or by truth table.

@lab(prove, bool, id=p3, pts=4, goal="A + AB = A")
@solution
A + AB = A by absorption
@end

@b{Fractions and integrals.} rat: algebra over the rationals, sqrt(c), and integrals of polynomials; givens and definitions go inside goal= separated by ;.

@lab(prove, rat, id=g0, goal="int_{0}^{1} x dx = 1/2")
@end

@b{Credit per step, and automation.} partial gives credit for each step that checks (otherwise all or nothing).

@lab(prove, id=p4, pts=4, partial, auto, goal="(a+1)^2 = a^2 + 2a + 1")
@end

@b{Graded.} The server re-checks the handed-in text with the same kernel; what the browser says is feedback only.

@section(Checked proofs in your notes)

Write a worked proof under a theorem and let the reader's browser check each step with IDoc's kernel, so a wrong step in your notes cannot go unnoticed.

@theorem(Square of a sum) For all natural numbers a and b, @eqi((a+b)^2 = a^2 + 2ab + b^2).
@end
@proof(check)
(a+b)^2 = (a+b)(a+b)        by ring
        = a^2 + 2ab + b^2   by ring
@end

@b{What it proves.} By default the theorem just above; goal= names the statement instead.

@proof(check, goal="(a+b)(a-b) = a^2 - b^2")
(a+b)(a-b) = a^2 - b^2   by ring
@end

@b{Induction.} induction n with base: and step: chains proves a statement for every n.

@theorem(Odd numbers) For every n, @eqi(sum_{i=0}^{n-1} (2i+1) = n^2).
@end
@proof(check)
induction n
step: sum_{i=0}^{n} (2i+1) = sum_{i=0}^{n-1} (2i+1) + (2n+1)   by sum
                           = n^2 + (2n+1)                        by IH
                           = (n+1)^2                             by ring
@end

@b{Graded.} Not a question: it is feedback for the reader.


@section(Every other argument)

@b{Chemistry hand-in and look.} submit=server keeps the student's answer, theme= sets the look, width= and height= size it, time= is the live-class window.

@chem(id=propane, submit=server, expect="C3H8 + 5O2 -> 3CO2 + 4H2O", theme=studio, width=600, height=200, time=5m)
C3H8 + O2 -> CO2 + H2O
@end

@b{Simulation look.} theme=, width=, height= and time= work as on every studio.

@sim(theme=dark, width=600, height=320, time=5m)
system: orbit
@end

@sim
system: double-pendulum
@end
